# CODEOWNERS — used by GitHub to auto-request reviews on PRs.
#
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners (GitHub
# usernames or team names). The last matching pattern wins.
#
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-customizations/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Replace <TEMPLATE-OWNER> with your GitHub username or team and uncomment.
# For a single-maintainer repo this is mostly informational; for a multi-
# maintainer repo it ensures the right people are pinged on PRs.

# Default owner for everything in the repo
# *  @<TEMPLATE-OWNER>

# Security-sensitive files require maintainer review
# /SECURITY.md             @<TEMPLATE-OWNER>
# /.github/workflows/      @<TEMPLATE-OWNER>
# /.github/dependabot.yml  @<TEMPLATE-OWNER>
